course: dictionary
lesson: 14935
title: Registration: a list, a call, or a number
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Registration means putting your name or details on an official list. In school, it is the time when the teacher calls out names to check who is there. «Our registration is at 8:45 every morning, when Miss Patel calls our names.»
explain: The word can also mean a number. «The car's registration is on the number plate.» In the UK, people often shorten it to «reg». Context tells you which meaning is right: look for clue words like form, club, car or morning.
explain: Clue words help you choose the meaning. «You need to complete the registration form before the club starts.» The words form and club tell you that registration means signing up.
fact: Registration means putting a name or details on an official list.
fact: In UK schools, registration is the start-of-day time when the register is taken.
fact: A car's registration is its number on the number plate. In the UK, people say «reg» for short.
fact: Useful phrases: «registration form», «registration number», «late registration», «online registration».
fact: To check your meaning, put it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «Our registration is at 8:45 every morning.» What is registration here? | A bag for books | A type of breakfast | *The time when the teacher checks who is in school | A race to the finish line
exercise: «Sam filled in the registration form for the swimming club.» What is a registration form for? | Taking a swimming test | *Signing up to join the club | Ordering lunch in the canteen | Writing a letter to Grandma
exercise: What does «late registration» mean? | Signing up before anyone else | Going to bed late | A slow car | *Signing up after the deadline
test: «The club will close registration on Friday.» What does closing registration mean? | Giving everyone a prize | Painting the club room | *Stopping people from signing up | Locking the car doors
test: In the UK, what does «reg» mean on a car? | A ticket for the car park | *The car's number on its number plate | The type of engine | A driving lesson
exam: Ben says, «Registration is the first lesson of the day.» Is he right? | Yes, it is maths | No, it is the end of the school day | Yes, it is lunch time | *No, it is the time the teacher calls names, not a lesson
